# Cloudflare Pages header rules.
# https://developers.cloudflare.com/pages/configuration/headers/

# Nothing is served out of a cache without asking us first. `no-cache` does not
# mean "do not store", it means "store it, but never use it without checking",
# which is what Ctrl+Shift+R does by hand: the reader always lands on the newest
# deploy. A file that has not changed comes back 304 with no body, so this costs
# one small conditional request per file rather than a download.
#
# There are no exceptions, artwork included. Pages merges every matching rule
# instead of letting the most specific one win, so a second block naming
# Cache-Control for /assets/img/* would send two contradictory values in one
# header and the browser would be free to pick either. One rule, no ambiguity.
#
# This governs copies fetched from now on. Anyone who was here before it landed
# still holds files under the old rules -- the item database was allowed to sit
# for a day -- and no header sent today can reach into a cache that is not
# asking. That is what the build stamp from tools/stamp_build.py is for: it
# changes the address, and an address the old cache has never seen cannot be
# answered from it.
/*
  Cache-Control: no-cache, must-revalidate
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), microphone=(), camera=(), interest-cohort=()
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains
